(THE CREATURES AT FULL SIZE) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(The roster is the spine of the collection game. It is planned at one hundred or) Tj
T*
(more species, built up over three chapters:) Tj
T*
T*
(Chapter One - thirty-six species) Tj
T*
(Chapter Two adds - thirty more) Tj
T*
(Chapter Three adds - thirty-four more) Tj
T*
(Full total - one hundred species) Tj
T*
T*
(All of it is built as data, not code. A creature is a row of numbers and a) Tj
T*
(sprite reference: name, types, base statistics, growth curve, learnset,) Tj
T*
(evolution, catch rate, rarity and habitat. The roster therefore grows by adding) Tj
T*
(entries rather than features, and balance changes are file edits rather than) Tj
T*
(rewrites.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(THE TWELVE TYPES) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(The type chart is our own, not borrowed: Ember, Tide, Verdant, Stone, Gale,) Tj
T*
(Spark, Frost, Shade, Radiance, Iron, Wild and Mind. Twelve is enough for a rich) Tj
T*
(set of strengths, weaknesses and immunities, and few enough that a player can) Tj
T*
(actually learn it. Every type has at least two strengths and is weak to at least) Tj
T*
(two others.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(WHAT EVERY CREATURE CARRIES) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(- six statistics: health, attack, defence, special attack, special defence, speed) Tj
T*
(- hidden individual values, so two of a species are never identical) Tj
T*
(- a nature from a table of twenty-five, favouring one stat and hindering another) Tj
T*
(- training values earned in battle, on a fixed budget) Tj
T*
(- at least one passive ability that fires on its own) Tj
T*
(- a rarity tier, and a place in a two- or three-stage evolution line) Tj
T*
(- a heritage record - see Lineage) Tj
ET
