(THE SYSTEMS - THE CORE DEPTH) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(These are the systems the game is not deep without. All are planned for the full) Tj
T*
(release, not a later one:) Tj
T*
T*
(- types and a full effectiveness chart) Tj
T*
(- the six statistics, with individual values, natures and training values) Tj
T*
(- passive abilities, at least one per species) Tj
T*
(- moves with power, accuracy, limited uses, priority, and a physical or special) Tj
T*
(  split) Tj
T*
(- five status conditions: Scorch, Blight, Static, Slumber and Chill) Tj
T*
(- statistic stages, six steps down to six steps up) Tj
T*
(- critical hits, damage variance and type multipliers) Tj
T*
(- held items with battle effects) Tj
T*
(- switching, a party of six, and storage beyond that) Tj
T*
(- double battles - needed for co-op, and used in single play too) Tj
T*
(- catching with tiered balls and a visible throw sequence) Tj
T*
(- experience, growth, learning moves on level, and evolution) Tj
T*
(- trainers, with their own teams and prize money) Tj
T*
(- an opponent that switches, heals, and plays to its type advantages) Tj
T*
(- day and night, weather, and terrain that matters) Tj
T*
(- breeding, with clear inheritance rules) Tj
T*
(- rare colourways that are heritable rather than random) Tj
T*
(- difficulty modes) Tj
T*
(- the dex, which is the collection game) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(THE STRETCH LIST) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Systems that make the game bigger rather than deeper, and come after the core:) Tj
T*
T*
(- a post-game battle facility, with streaks and prizes) Tj
T*
(- move tutors, machines, and egg moves) Tj
T*
(- fishing and foraging) Tj
T*
(- in-game trades) Tj
T*
(- legendary creatures, found once) Tj
T*
(- rewards for completing the dex) Tj
T*
(- trainer rematches) Tj
T*
(- contests and a photo mode) Tj
T*
(- version exclusives, tied to trading) Tj
ET
