1 0 0 1 72 716 Tm
(THE SIGNATURE MECHANIC - LINEAGE) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Every memorable game in this genre is remembered for the one thing it does) Tj
T*
(differently. Ours is Lineage, and it is the reason to play this one.) Tj
T*
T*
(Most games give you a rare colour variant that is random and cannot be) Tj
T*
(influenced. Ours is heritable, and that single change turns a lottery into a) Tj
T*
(project.) Tj
T*
T*
(Every creature carries a permanent, visible record of where it came from and) Tj
T*
(what it inherited. It has three parts:) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 11 Tf
(Heritage traits) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(Inherited, and they affect battle. Breeding combines the parents' traits under) Tj
T*
(clear rules, so chaining generations produces combinations that do not exist in) Tj
T*
(the wild at all.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 11 Tf
(Marks) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(Visible patterns and colours that show ancestry. Because Marks are heritable, a) Tj
T*
(player can breed toward the look they want instead of hoping for it.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 11 Tf
(Origin) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(The wild area it came from, or the player whose line it descends from, shown as) Tj
T*
(a small family tree on the creature's card.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(WHY THIS MATTERS MORE FOR US THAN FOR ANYONE ELSE) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Breeding generates near-infinite variety from data. It costs no new art, no new) Tj
T*
(sprites and no new code - only combinations. It is the one axis where a small) Tj
T*
(team can genuinely out-produce a large studio, and it is the engine that keeps) Tj
T*
(the collection game alive for years.) Tj
T*
T*
(It also changes what trading means. A trade is not swapping a stat block. It is) Tj
T*
(swapping a history, and that is what makes a collection emotional rather than) Tj
T*
(arithmetic.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
