(THE DRIFT) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Released creatures do not simply vanish. They drift into other players' worlds) Tj
T*
(with their lineage attached, so a player can meet someone else's bloodline in) Tj
T*
(their own grass. Breeding, releasing, trading and exploring become one loop, and) Tj
T*
(exploration gains a reason beyond your own collection.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(MULTIPLAYER, TRADING AND VERSIONS) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Two players can share a battle, cooperatively. That is rare in this genre and it) Tj
T*
(is a deliberate differentiator - and the battle engine is built around a list of) Tj
T*
(participants from the first day, so co-op is not a rewrite.) Tj
T*
T*
(Trading is live and in-room. Both players hold their confirm button at the same) Tj
T*
(moment for a trade to complete, so a trade can never happen by accident.) Tj
T*
T*
(The game ships as two versions, Dawn and Dusk. Most creatures appear in both, and) Tj
T*
(each version has a handful of exclusives. That gives trading a real purpose, and) Tj
T*
(gives the multiplayer room a reason to exist beyond battling.) Tj
T*
T*
(Multiplayer is always an enhancement and never a dependency. If the connection) Tj
T*
(is down, the game still starts, plays and saves alone.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(HOW IT SHIPS - THREE CHAPTERS) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Chapter One is a complete game of roughly ten to twelve hours: four badge) Tj
T*
(challenges, about twenty areas, thirty-six creatures and two field powers, with) Tj
T*
(its own beginning, middle and ending, and threads deliberately left open.) Tj
T*
T*
(Chapter One - four challenges, about twenty areas, thirty-six creatures) Tj
T*
(Chapter Two adds - three challenges, ten areas, thirty creatures) Tj
T*
(Chapter Three adds - one challenge and the league, eight areas, thirty-four) Tj
T*
(  creatures) Tj
T*
(Full total - eight challenges plus the league, about thirty-eight areas, one) Tj
T*
(  hundred creatures, five field powers) Tj
T*
T*
(Each chapter resolves its own story and ships finished. Stopping after any one) Tj
T*
(of them is never a loss, which is what makes a plan this size survivable.) Tj
ET
endstream
