(PRESENTATION - THE LOOK) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(The target is HD-2D: hand-drawn pixel creatures standing in a three-dimensional) Tj
T*
(world, with a shallow depth of field that makes the scene look like a small) Tj
T*
(diorama, plus real lighting, glow and drifting particles. It is exactly what) Tj
T*
(a Game Boy game, remade means today, and it is what makes a browser game look) Tj
T*
(like a premium product rather than a tribute.) Tj
T*
T*
(It is also a rendering layer rather than a different game. The world stays a) Tj
T*
(grid of tiles underneath, so the ambitious part cannot break the part that) Tj
T*
(works. It is planned as a deliberate late stage, with a graphics setting that) Tj
T*
(falls back to flat, crisp pixel art if a device struggles.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(HOW IT GETS BUILT) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(The work is staged so that every stage ends with something playable:) Tj
T*
T*
(0. Skeleton - the overworld, one map, one encounter, one battle) Tj
T*
(1. Battle depth - types, moves, abilities, status, identity, catching, growth) Tj
T*
(2. World systems - many maps, non-player characters, dialogue, trainers, shops) Tj
T*
(3. Content - the full roster, moves, encounter tables, the dex) Tj
T*
(4. Progression - the challenges, field powers, the rival, the plot, the ending) Tj
T*
(5. Presentation - HD-2D, audio, animation, and performance on real devices) Tj
T*
(6. Multiplayer - co-op battles over a live room, then trading) Tj
T*
(7. Endgame - the battle facility, leaderboards, accessibility, polish) Tj
T*
T*
(Stages 0 and 1 are done and playable. Stage 2 is in progress.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(ART AND COST) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Art is planned to cost approximately nothing, which is what makes a roster of a) Tj
T*
(hundred creatures realistic rather than a wish:) Tj
T*
T*
(- public-domain sprite packs for the first creatures, licence-clean and free) Tj
T*
(- creatures assembled from parts on a shared palette, so variety comes from data) Tj
T*
(  rather than drawing) Tj
T*
(- a small number of painted poster pieces for bosses and box art) Tj
T*
T*
(The look is held together by one shared palette and one tile grid, so every) Tj
T*
(source sits in the same world.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(WHAT IT IS NOT) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Honesty matters more than optimism here. This is not, and will not be, a match) Tj
T*
(for the biggest games in the genre on content volume - those are built by) Tj
